# 003 · No default spend limit for advisors

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

The advisors' daily spend limit (`max_usd_per_day`) has no default. A limit applies only when someone sets it.

## Why

No default caps is a rule for every goal. Before this goal, advisors stopped at 20 USD a day unless configured otherwise.

## Done when

- [ ] `max_usd_per_day` is optional, and advisors apply it only when it is set.
- [ ] A test shows that advisors run with no limit when none is set.
- [ ] The settings docs say so.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: No cap by default. Anyone who wants a limit can configure one.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-19: Built on the development branch; the commit is next.

